 >> [speaking in Chinese]

240
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:48,000
 >> So they keep the smallest law, but they break the largest one.

241
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:53,000
 >> [speaking in Chinese]

242
00:20:53,000 --> 00:21:13,000
 >> [speaking in Chinese]

243
00:21:13,000 --> 00:21:16,000
 >> So we can now answer our three questions.

244
00:21:16,000 --> 00:21:19,000
 First, why did no one put him into the pool for 38 years?

245
00:21:19,000 --> 00:21:25,000
 Because under a rule of "fast enough, useful enough," he counted for nothing.

246
00:21:25,000 --> 00:21:28,000
 And yet he never once went into the pool.

247
00:21:28,000 --> 00:21:31,000
 What healed him was not the water, but Jesus who walked over and asked,

248
00:21:31,000 --> 00:21:33,000
 "Do you want to be healed?"

249
00:21:33,000 --> 00:21:46,000
 >> [speaking in Chinese]

250
00:21:46,000 --> 00:21:57,000
 >> [speaking in Chinese]

251
00:21:57,000 --> 00:22:00,000
 >> And second, why on the Sabbath, and why carry the man?

252
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:03,000
 Because the Sabbath was never about stopping to work,

253
00:22:03,000 --> 00:22:07,000
 but about restoring people to the goodness of God's creation.

254
00:22:07,000 --> 00:22:12,000
 The man that carried him for 38 years is now carried by him,

255
00:22:12,000 --> 00:22:17,000
 turned before the whole city from a sign of abandonment into a sign of healing.

256
00:22:17,000 --> 00:22:36,000
 >> [speaking in Chinese]

257
00:22:36,000 --> 00:22:39,000
 >> And third, what does "my father is working until now" mean?

258
00:22:39,000 --> 00:22:43,000
 Because God has not stopped working for a single day since the creation.

259
00:22:43,000 --> 00:22:46,000
 And the work that Jesus does is the Father's own work,

260
00:22:46,000 --> 00:22:51,000
 which the Jews understood as making himself equal with God.

261
00:22:51,000 --> 00:23:04,000
 >> [speaking in Chinese]

262
00:23:04,000 --> 00:23:08,000
 >> So brothers and sisters, we need to ask ourselves one question today.

263
00:23:08,000 --> 00:23:12,000
 Are we like the self-righteous police where we keep all the rules

264
00:23:12,000 --> 00:23:16,000
 while people besides us that have been lying there for 38 years,

265
00:23:16,000 --> 00:23:19,000
 but we never once ask them a single question?

266
00:23:19,000 --> 00:23:48,000
 >> [speaking in Chinese]

267
00:23:48,000 --> 00:23:51,000
 >> Whether you have been coming to church for many years or you just began,

268
00:23:51,000 --> 00:23:54,000
 if you call yourself a disciple of Jesus,

269
00:23:54,000 --> 00:23:58,000
 our Christian's identity does not rest on a checklist of behavior

270
00:23:58,000 --> 00:24:03,000
 or complicated words in prayer or on how many Sunday service you have to attend.

271
00:24:03,000 --> 00:24:06,000
 It simply rests on the relationship with Jesus.

272
00:24:06,000 --> 00:24:10,000
 And because of this relationship, we can pray to God honestly.

273
00:24:10,000 --> 00:24:14,000
 And because of this relationship, even when it is inconvenient for us,

274
00:24:14,000 --> 00:24:19,000
 we still check in on the people around us rather than keeping the love of Jesus to ourselves.

275
00:24:19,000 --> 00:24:42,000
 >> [speaking in Chinese]

276
00:24:42,000 --> 00:24:45,000
 >> And if we only judge people by the world standard,

277
00:24:45,000 --> 00:24:48,000
 which is productivity, money, or status,

278
00:24:48,000 --> 00:24:50,000
 we will always stay inside our little bubble.

279
00:24:50,000 --> 00:24:53,000
 And the gospel that we share or the care that we have for others

280
00:24:53,000 --> 00:24:57,000
 will never be experienced by people outside of our circle.

281
00:24:57,000 --> 00:25:10,000
 >> [speaking in Chinese]

282
00:25:10,000 --> 00:25:13,000
 >> And that is precisely the irony of our passage today.

283
00:25:13,000 --> 00:25:16,000
 In a place called the house of steadfast love,

284
00:25:16,000 --> 00:25:21,000
 for 38 years, no one cared to say a single word to this man who was in guilt.

285
00:25:21,000 --> 00:25:24,000
 But Jesus walked towards him and reached out to him.

286
00:25:24,000 --> 00:25:27,000
 He sent an example, and for us who follow him,

287
00:25:27,000 --> 00:25:30,000
 we can learn from Jesus' example together.

288
00:25:30,000 --> 00:25:31,000
 >> [speaking in Chinese]

289
00:25:31,000 --> 00:25:32,000
 >> Let's pray together.

290
00:25:32,000 --> 00:25:53,000
 >> [speaking in Chinese]

291
00:25:53,000 --> 00:25:57,000
 >> Heavenly Father, thank you for being patient with us all the time.

292
00:25:57,000 --> 00:26:02,000
 Even with all our misunderstanding of you, you still speak to us patiently,

293
00:26:02,000 --> 00:26:06,000
 waiting for the day that we will wake up to your truth.

294
00:26:06,000 --> 00:26:13,000
 >> [speaking in Chinese]

295
00:26:13,000 --> 00:26:16,000
 >> Give us once again the chance to make a fresh start,

296
00:26:16,000 --> 00:26:21,000
 to see ourselves as well as the people around us through your standard.

297
00:26:21,000 --> 00:26:24,000
 >> [speaking in Chinese]

298
00:26:24,000 --> 00:26:26,000
 >> In the name of Jesus Christ, we pray.

299
00:26:26,000 --> 00:26:30,000
 Amen. Welcome to UE.

